<section class="page">
  <div class="header"><b>Evidence boundary</b><span>Acquisition and preprocessing</span></div>
  <h2>One public signal, five deliberately observable counties</h2>
  <p class="callout">The design starts with the scoring source itself, then treats every absent record as unknown—not as proof of zero outage.</p>
  <div class="grid2">
    <div>
      <h3>Source and spatial key</h3>
      <p>EAGLE-I v4 supplies county outage counts at a nominal 15-minute cadence. `MCC.csv` supplies the organizer-linked fixed customer denominator. We join only on the zero-padded five-digit FIPS code; county and state strings are explanatory fields, never keys.</p>
      <p>The chosen set spans one Midwestern metropolitan system and four Northeast systems. Large customer bases reduce ratio quantization; repeated 2023–2025 coverage supports rolling-state construction; the New York / New Jersey cluster also permits a contemporaneous regional context signal.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card tight">
      <h3>Preprocessing decisions</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Parse raw timestamps as UTC and collapse exact duplicate county/timestamp rows by mean.</li>
        <li>Task A target for validation: mean of available quarter-hour values in the hour ending at the hourly target.</li>
        <li>Task B target: native 15-minute observation.</li>
        <li>Do not densify an absent target to zero; exclude it from local metric denominators.</li>
        <li>At inference, last-observation and lag features use only timestamps at or before the issue time.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <table><thead><tr><th>FIPS</th><th>County</th><th>State</th><th>MCC customers</th><th>Selection role</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for c in counties %}<tr><td>{{ c.fips_code }}</td><td>{{ c.county }}</td><td>{{ c.state }}</td><td>{{ c.customers_fmt }}</td><td>{{ c.role }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>
  <img class="figure medium" src="figures/coverage.svg">
  <p class="caption">Observed EAGLE-I rows divided by nominal quarter-hour slots. The rising coverage is why missing rows remain explicit rather than being confused with zero-customer outages.</p>
  <div class="footer"><span>Tideglass · {{ team_name }}</span><span>02 / 07</span></div>
</section>

<section class="page">
  <div class="header"><b>Exploration</b><span>Signals translated into controls</span></div>
  <h2>Persistence is strong; magnitudes are not well behaved</h2>
  <div class="grid2">
    <div>
      <p class="callout">The median adjacent-quarter log correlation is {{ median_corr }}, while each county’s 99th percentile is many times its routine median.</p>
      <p>This combination argues against a single unconstrained level regression. Tideglass separates the stable part of the process—county scale, seasonality and recurrence—from an issue-time renewal path that can carry an active event into the short horizon.</p>
      <h3>Feature families</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Current state:</b> last value, staleness, 1-hour median, 6-hour mean/max/trend.</li>
        <li><b>Slow state:</b> 24-hour median/max and 7-day median / 90th / 99th percentiles.</li>
        <li><b>Recurrence:</b> causal 1-, 7- and 14-day values with missing indicators.</li>
        <li><b>Geometry:</b> lead, square-root/log lead, issue hour, target hour and day-of-year cycles.</li>
        <li><b>Spatial context:</b> the median current ratio across the same five counties.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div><img class="figure tall" src="figures/exploration.svg"><p class="caption">Left: adjacent-quarter persistence on log counts. Right: p99-to-median magnitude ratio (capped visually at 120×). Both are computed before the 2025 test window where applicable.</p></div>
  </div>
  <img class="figure medium" src="figures/feature_layers.svg">
  <div class="note"><b>Why no weather feature?</b> The organizer requires genuine forecasts available at each issue time; target-time observations or stitched hindsight weather would leak. The system uses an auditable outage-renewal path rather than an incomplete archive. The limitation is explicit: an unseen event onset cannot be anticipated until it appears in available telemetry.</div>
  <div class="footer"><span>Tideglass · {{ team_name }}</span><span>03 / 07</span></div>
</section>

<section class="page">
  <div class="header"><b>Method</b><span>Model and inference</span></div>
  <h2>Two convex heads, renewal, and historical MAE calibration</h2>
  <img class="figure tall" src="figures/model_pipeline.svg">
  <div class="grid2 tight">
    <div>
      <h3>Task A · structural renewal</h3>
      <p>A task-specific Ridge pipeline predicts `log1p(customers_out)` for +1h through +48h. One-hot county and lead bands combine with standardized continuous features. Long leads naturally lean on slow state, recurrence and calendar structure; no direct persistence override is applied.</p>
      <h3>Task B · short-horizon renewal</h3>
      <p>The same regularized convex family is fitted at +15m through +6h. The output is blended with 20% of the last available outage count. That weight was fixed before the sealed release and improves the forward replays’ short-horizon tail behavior.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Imbalance handling</h3>
      <p>Outage magnitude is long-tailed rather than cleanly binary. The log target limits domination by rare extremes. Sample weight `1 + min(log1p(y)/10, 1.5)` gives large events up to 2.5× influence while keeping routine intervals central to MAE.</p>
      <h3>Historical MAE calibration</h3>
      <p>A groupwise weighted-median scale corrects the Ridge heads' positive-event magnitude for MAE: county × lead for Task A, and lead with 500-row shrinkage for Task B. The form was selected on the 2023 forward replay, evaluated once on untouched 2024, then refit from historical 2024 out-of-fold predictions for the sealed model.</p>
      <h3>Projection</h3>
      <p>Calibrated counts are divided by the county-specific MCC customer count and clipped to `[0,1]`. The model emits a continuous ratio; it never rounds back to customer lattice points.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="grid3"><div class="card"><strong class="metric">206,818</strong><span>final Task-A training rows</span></div><div class="card"><strong class="metric">407,603</strong><span>final Task-B training rows</span></div><div class="card"><strong class="metric">41,729</strong><span>fixed seed</span></div></div>
