</section>

<section class="page">
  <div class="header"><b>Evidence</b><span>Temporal validation and ablation</span></div>
  <h2>Untouched forward replay confirms the calibrated release</h2>
  <p>The Sep–Nov 2023 expanding-window replay selects the declared calibration form; the untouched Sep–Nov 2024 replay evaluates it. Every replay trains only on earlier information, and missing EAGLE-I targets are excluded rather than invented. These are local public-data diagnostics—not an organizer or leaderboard score.</p>
  <img class="figure tall" src="figures/validation.svg">
  <table><thead><tr><th>2024 replay</th><th>Task</th><th>Rows</th><th>MAE</th><th>RMSE</th><th>Top-decile MAE</th><th>Correlation</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for row in validation_rows %}<tr><td>{{ row.method }}</td><td>{{ row.task_id }}</td><td>{{ row.rows }}</td><td>{{ row.mae }}</td><td>{{ row.rmse }}</td><td>{{ row.tail }}</td><td>{{ row.corr }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>
  <p class="caption">Error units are outage-ratio points. Full fold and method records—including bias, p95 absolute error and correlation—are packaged in `artifacts/validation_metrics.csv`.</p>
  <div class="grid2">
    <div class="card"><h3>Task A result</h3><p>Against last observation, the full model lowers 2024 MAE by {{ a_mae_gain }} and RMSE by {{ a_rmse_gain }}. Calibration further lowers MAE versus the frozen structural head while retaining its lead/calendar signal.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Task B result</h3><p>The renewal-plus-calibration path lowers MAE by {{ b_mae_gain }} and RMSE by {{ b_rmse_gain }} versus last observation. Calibration also improves MAE and correlation versus the pre-calibration output, with a modest top-decile MAE tradeoff.</p></div>
