<section class="page">
  <div class="header"><b>Release</b><span>Contract and causal audit</span></div>
  <h2>The submitted file is a frozen inference product</h2>
  <div class="grid2">
    <div><img class="figure tall" src="figures/causal_audit.svg"></div>
    <div>
      <h3>Exact row universe</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Task A:</b> 92 daily issues × 5 counties × 48 hourly leads = 22,080.</li>
        <li><b>Task B:</b> 365 six-hourly issues × 5 counties × 24 quarter-hour leads = 43,800.</li>
        <li>Primary key: task, FIPS, issue time, target time.</li>
        <li>All timestamps are canonical UTC; every ratio is finite and within bounds.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Leakage control</h3>
      <p>Every frozen row stores the latest source timestamp used. An executable assertion verifies `max_source_timestamp ≤ issue_time`. A target can overlap another batch and remains a separate scored row. The inference file contains features and keys, but no target label.</p>
      <h3>Prediction distribution</h3>
      <img class="figure short" src="figures/prediction_distribution.svg">
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="note"><b>Release binding.</b> Model, input and output hashes are validated before packaging. Frozen inference regenerates the submitted CSV byte for byte; retraining is not part of that reproduction path.</div>
